# What in this directory is worth keeping.
#
# The data disk mixes two very different things: material a human curates —
# character, memories, custom agents, model choices — and runtime state that is
# regenerated, enormous, or secret. Only the first kind is tracked.
#
# This is an ALLOWLIST, and deliberately so. Ignore-by-default means anything a
# future release starts writing here is untracked until someone decides
# otherwise, which is the safe direction to fail: a new state file that nobody
# added to this list is merely missing from a commit, whereas a new secret that
# nobody added would be committed forever.
#
# `git log` over this repository is what tells you whether an upgrade changed
# something you had customised, and `git bundle create ../steward.bundle --all`
# is a complete, portable export of it.

# Everything, unless re-included below.
/*

!/.gitignore
!/.steward-version
!/SOUL.md
!/agents/
!/config/
!/memories/
!/profiles/
!/skills/
!/wiki/

# config.yaml is NOT tracked, though it is exactly the kind of file that
# belongs here. It carries the dashboard secret and password hash, and it
# records absolute host paths that are true of this box and no other. Copying
# one to a second machine would move a credential and break the tool sandbox
# at the same time.
#
# Profile configs are cloned from it and carry the same secret.
/profiles/*/config.yaml

# State that can appear underneath a tracked directory.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
